  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Crossing and finishing",
  "description": "A winger dribbles along the touchline towards the byline and crosses. Two forwards start centrally outside the penalty area and time their runs: one to the near post and one to the far post. Finish against a goalkeeper.\n\nRun it from both wings. Add a defender when the players are ready, and vary the cross: driven along the ground, lofted to the far post, or cut back to the penalty spot. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Winger: look up before crossing and play the ball into the space the forwards are running into."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Forwards: hold your run so you arrive in the space at the same time as the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "One goes to the near post, one to the far post – never on the same line."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Finish with the inside of the foot, or head the ball down towards the ground."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
